    "body": "RELEX Solutions has acquired autone, a London-based company that helps fashion, sports, and lifestyle brands plan their inventory. It's RELEX's seventh acquisition.\nWhat’s Related\nAutone will become the core of a new business unit called RELEX Lifestyle, focused on fashion, sports and lifestyle retail . Alex Chataigner will lead the new unit.\nFounded in 2021, autone helps brands make better buying, allocation, and replenishment decisions over the course of a season. Its team includes former merchandisers, inventory planners, and data scientists who worked at fashion and luxury brands. Customers include Roberto Cavalli, Cult Gaia, Vilebrequin, Lancel, IKKS, and the jewelry division of Galeries Lafayette. The Kooples recently picked autone for buying and allocation on its seasonal collections, and British luxury brand Sunspel is using it to automate replenishment and rebalancing across its stores worldwide.\nRELATED: Supply Chain Leaders Give Their AI Readiness a 4.9 Out of 10 Score\nThe challenge of planning in fashion\nFashion is hard to plan. New collections often have no sales history, buying decisions happen months before products reach stores, and the window to sell at full price can be short.\nAutone forecasts demand using product attributes and how similar items sold in past collections. It predicts demand down to the product, store, size, and color. That helps teams buy smarter before a season starts and move inventory around as demand shifts.\nOne French luxury leather goods brand cut its rebalancing time by 90%, from two and a half days to two hours, and reported a 10% revenue increase.\n“We founded autone because we lived it firsthand. Before autone, we did this job inside luxury houses: the endless firefighting, collections overproduced and heading for markdowns, shortages that left stores empty, and brilliant teams patching a broken system with spreadsheets. So we built the tool we wished we had,” said Adil Bouhdadi, CEO of autone.\nOne system for many products\nRELEX says the deal gives fashion retailers one engine for both seasonal and continuous ranges, with one interface and one partner . That covers everything from financial and assortment planning through markdowns, clearance, rebalancing, and buying.\n“Fashion retail has unique planning challenges that require a deep understanding of how the industry operates,” said Mikko Kärkkäinen, Group CEO and co-founder of RELEX Solutions. “The autone team brings that expertise, along with technology developed specifically for the decisions fashion retailers make every day.”\nIntersport France already uses RELEX to pull its planning into one system, and it sees autone as a good addition. “The fashion and sports expertise from autone complements this approach, helping our retailers buy closer to real demand throughout the season,” said Gérard Leclerc, President, Belgium, Spain and Portugal, Intersport France.",
